   "evidence": "The proof uses nontriviality only to get `norm_pos_iff.mpr one_ne_zero` for `div_le_iff\u2080`. Mathlib has `div_le_of_le_mul\u2080 (hb : 0 \u2264 b) (hc : 0 \u2264 c) (h : a \u2264 c * b) : a / b \u2264 c` (grep hit: Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Triangle/Counting.lean:52), which needs only nonnegativity. The premise `\u2016a\u2016 \u2264 \u2016T\u2016 * \u20161\u2016` is exactly `norm_leftRegularRenormEquiv_symm_le` after `symm_apply_apply`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Normed/Algebra/LeftRegularRenorm.lean",
   "fix": "Drop `[Nontrivial A]` and prove it as `div_le_of_le_mul\u2080 (norm_nonneg _) (norm_nonneg _) (by simpa only [ContinuousAlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply] using norm_leftRegularRenormEquiv_symm_le \ud835\udd5c A (leftRegularRenormEquiv \ud835\udd5c A a))`.",
   "issue": "`div_norm_one_le_norm_leftRegularRenormEquiv` assumes `[Nontrivial A]`, which is stronger than needed. When `A` is the zero algebra, `\u2016(1 : A)\u2016 = 0`, so `\u2016a\u2016 / \u20161\u2016 = 0 \u2264 \u2016_\u2016`. The PR description's claim that nontriviality is required for this bound is also wrong.",
